 "id": 180536,
 "name": "W3C Open Source Program Community Group",
 "is_closed": false,
 "creation-date": "2026-10-21",
 "description": "<p>In September 2026, W3C <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/blog/2026/w3c-launches-first-pilot-of-program-to-support-open-source-projects/\">announced</a> a first pilot project for a new Open Source Program. </p>\n\n<p>The mission of the W3C Open Source Program Community Group is to manage the next phase of growth of a W3C Open Source Program.\nThis Community Group will study what is needed to create a scalable W3C Open Source Program, focusing on program governance, operations, and liaisons, and developing a clear project lifecycle description. </p>\n\n<p>The group has a goal for W3C to launch a full Open Source Program by mid-2028, after which the expectation is that this Community Group would be replaced by a governing body (and therefore archived).</p>\n\n<p>This group will not publish Specifications.</p>",
